  "notes": [
    "grain secret: the SLIP-0010 node m/44'/1010'/account'/3'/0'; a grain's key: Ed25519 from the seed BLAKE3-derive_key(\"Salarium grain key v1\", secret || slug)",
    "manifest: Borsh of GrainManifest; owner: AccountId [20]; owner_key: Ed25519 tag 0 [32] | P256 tag 1 [33] (SEC1 compressed); id = derive_key(\"Salarium grain manifest id v1\", borsh); the owner key signs m = derive_key(\"Salarium grain manifest v1\", borsh): Ed25519 over m, or ECDSA P-256 over SHA-256 of m as r || s with a low s",
    "managed: the owner is the kind 5 account of accounts-v1.json and the owner key its phone (phone_secret_hex there); P-256 signatures here are RFC 6979's, any valid low-s signature checks",
    "json: the form a hosted grain serves at /.well-known/salarium-grain; bytes in lowercase hex",
    "icon = derive_key(\"Salarium grain icon v1\", png); bundle = derive_key(\"Salarium grain bundle v1\", zip)",
    "login: the grain key signs derive_key(\"Salarium grain login v1\", Borsh(GrainLogin))",
    "invoice: the signer signs derive_key(\"Salarium grain invoice v1\", genesis_hash || Borsh(Invoice)); a certified key's InvoiceKeyCert is signed by the owner over derive_key(\"Salarium grain invoice key v1\", Borsh((slug, key, expires_at)))",
    "the payment's public memo: the reference in lowercase hex, a space, the invoice's text",
    "grain messaging key: X25519 secret derive_key(\"Salarium grain messaging key v1\", secret || slug); frames to a grain alias are base64url(nonce 24 || NaCl crypto_box) between messaging keys",
    "notification: the owner or the certified server key signs derive_key(\"Salarium grain notification v1\", genesis_hash || Borsh(GrainNotification)); SignedGrainNotification is Borsh {notification, cert: Option<InvoiceKeyCert>, signature}",
    "registry: Action::Registry is tag 1 {call, amount: u64}; the calls after ExchangeDebt (tag 6) are RegisterGrain tag 7 {manifest: SignedGrainManifest}, paid in SALT, at least the slug's deposit (deposits below), kept up to 100 SALT; UpdateGrain tag 8 {manifest}; RetireGrain tag 9 {slug: String}; the sender is the manifest's owner, and its owner_key speaks for it (13-accounts §5); ids as in transaction-v3.json",
    "app studio (24-app-studio): Entry tag 2 Chat (no fields; JSON {\"chat\": {}}), notifications only; ConfigureGrain tag 34 {slug, servers: Vec<[u8;32]> (0-4, valid Ed25519, distinct, each one live grain's only), category: u8 (0-9)}, protocol version 1 only; ConfigureGrain tag 39 {slug, servers: Vec<ServerKeyProof {key [32], proof [64]}>, category: u8}, from protocol version 2: each key signs (strict Ed25519) derive_key(\"Salarium grain server v1\", Borsh((genesis_hash [32], slug: String, owner: AccountId [20]))) for the call's sender as owner (signed_payload_hex is that Borsh); SetGrainAccess tag 36 {slug, public: bool, members: Vec<(AccountId, u8 roles: 1 user, 2 developer, 4 viewer)> (0-64, distinct, not the owner)}; RateGrain tag 37 {slug, score: u8 (1-5, 0 withdraws), review: String (at most 140 characters, no control characters)} by any account but the owner; BindHandle tag 35 is in handles-v1.json",
    "donations (24-app-studio §2b): SetGrainDonations tag 76 {slug: String, open: bool (Borsh 1 or 0)}, amount 0, from protocol version 9 (a block of an earlier version carries no tag 76): the owner of a live grain opens or closes its donations, off until opened and dropped when it retires; grain_get shows donations; a donation is an ordinary transfer to the grain's owner (grain_get's owner), never to an address typed anywhere",
    "a registered server key signs a notification with cert None, as the owner key does: a wallet checks it against the owner key and the server keys of the grain's registry record (by-registered-key, registered_servers)",
    "a registered server key signs an invoice with cert None too, and only to the grain's owner (invoices.registered): a wallet reads the grain's registry record at its canonical beacon block, refuses any invoice of a retired grain (retired), tries the owner key, then each key the record names (signature when none verifies), and takes a server key's invoice only when to is the record's owner (payee); a certified key's invoice is checked as before, any payee",
    "developer key: salarium-app:1:<hrp>:<first 8 bytes of the genesis hash, hex>:<slug>:<the server key's Ed25519 secret, hex>, lower case, nothing else"
  ],
